if there's a pump widget on the main page\n2. The \"马达3\" (motor 3) tag doesn't exist as a point\n\nI should ask the user for clarification:\n- Does the pump widget already exist? What's its widget_id?\n- Does the motor 3 point exist? If not, should I create it first?\n- What type of point is motor 3 (analog, digital)?\n- Which property should be bound?\n\nActually, let me think about this differently. The user might be using informal language:\n- \"泵1\" could be a widget_id like \"pump_1\" or \"pump1\"\n- \"马达3\" could be a tag like \"MOTOR_3\" or \"motor3\"\n\nI should ask the user for clarification since:\n1. There are no points defined - \"马达3\" (motor 3) doesn't exist as a tag\n2. I don't know the widget_id of \"泵1\"\n3. I don't know which property to bind\n\nLet me ask the user for more details."}], "rag": {"enabled": false, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 12, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": false, "selected_workflow": null}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 19402, "output_tokens": 862, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 30223.14890002599}, "judge": null}
