l, it requires an existing analog point to attach the alarm to. The description says \"Create an analog alarm with high/low limits on an existing analog point.\"\n\nSince the point NO_SUCH_TEMP doesn't exist, I should:\n1. First check if the point exists by listing points or trying to create the alarm\n2. If it doesn't exist, inform the user that they need to create the point first\n\nLet me first try to list the points to verify, or I can inform the user directly that the point needs to exist first. Actually, the user already told me the point doesn't exist, so I should explain that they need to create the point first before creating an alarm on it.\n\nHowever, let me be helpful - I should inform the user that the alarm cannot be created on a non-existent point, and offer to create the point first if they want."}], "rag": {"enabled": false, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 12, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": false, "selected_workflow": null}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 9543, "output_tokens": 484, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 12804.107200005092}, "judge": null}
